1. NVIDIA NV-Segment-CTMR (VISTA3D)  --  the encoder backbone
================================================================================

  Source     https://huggingface.co/nvidia/NV-Segment-CTMR
  Licence    NVIDIA OneWay Non-Commercial License          [VERIFIED]
             (the model card states the model is for academic research and
             development only; commercial use is not permitted. The associated
             CODE is Apache-2.0, but the WEIGHTS are not.)

  These weights are NOT redistributed here. They are downloaded by the user.

  The authors accept the non-commercial restriction: this release is for
  academic research and no commercial licence is being sought from NVIDIA.

  CONSEQUENCE FOR THIS RELEASE: the end-to-end pipeline cannot
  be used commercially. The surrogate consumes a feature pyramid that only
  these weights can produce, so the non-commercial restriction reaches the
  whole system, not merely the backbone.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. weights/fm_encoder/  --  our LoRA adapter and STRD block
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  adapter_model.safetensors is a low-rank delta on specific NV-Segment-CTMR
  layers and is meaningless without them. It is therefore distributed on the
  same non-commercial terms as the backbone it modifies.

  Whether a LoRA adapter is legally a derivative work is unsettled. This
  repository takes the conservative reading. Anyone wanting a different one
  should obtain it from NVIDIA and from their own institution, not from here.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. weights/phomineuro_s{0,1,2}.pt  --  the surrogate
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Trained by the authors on their own Monte-Carlo simulations. Contains no
  third-party parameters. Offered under CC BY 4.0.

  It is nonetheless unusable on its own: it consumes the 1488-channel pyramid
  from section 1. A CC BY 4.0 file inside a non-commercial pipeline is still
  inside a non-commercial pipeline.

